def build_immigration_alert(site_key, service, city, state):
    # Merged into build_trending_alert — suppressed here to avoid duplication
    return ""

    return f"""<div class="imm-alert">
  <div class="imm-alert-badge">{_si("warning",12)} 2025–2026 Enforcement Update</div>
  <div class="imm-alert-head">ICE Enforcement Has Increased — Know Your Rights in {city}</div>
  <div class="imm-alert-body">ICE enforcement operations have significantly increased across the US since early 2025, including in {city}. If you or a family member has been detained, received a notice to appear, or is at risk of deportation, time is critical. An immigration attorney can file emergency motions, request bonds, and challenge removal orders — but only if contacted immediately.</div>
  <div class="imm-alert-items">
    <div class="imm-alert-item"><span>{_si("stop",16)}</span><span><strong>If detained:</strong> You have the right to remain silent and the right to an attorney. Do not sign any documents before speaking with a lawyer.</span></div>
    <div class="imm-alert-item"><span>{_si("document",16)}</span><span><strong>Notice to Appear (NTA):</strong> If you've received an NTA, you have limited time to respond. An attorney can file a motion to change venue or request a bond hearing.</span></div>
    <div class="imm-alert-item"><span>{_si("house",16)}</span><span><strong>Know your home rights:</strong> ICE generally cannot enter your home without a judicial warrant signed by a judge — not just an administrative warrant.</span></div>
    <div class="imm-alert-item"><span>{_si("alert",16)}</span><span><strong>Emergency representation:</strong> Many {city} immigration attorneys offer same-day emergency consultations for detention cases. Average cost: {fmt(int(1000 * (1 + (hash(city) % 30) / 100)))}–{fmt(int(2500 * (1 + (hash(city) % 30) / 100)))} for emergency representation.</span></div>
    <div class="imm-alert-item"><span>{_si("chat",16)}</span><span><strong>AILA {state} chapter</strong> can refer you to qualified immigration attorneys in {city}: aila.org/find-immigration-lawyer</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="imm-alert-disc">This information is for general guidance only — not legal advice. Always consult a licensed immigration attorney for your specific situation. Laws and enforcement priorities change frequently.</div>
</div>"""


