        imm_context_map = {'New York': "NYC's immigration courts at 26 Federal Plaza are among the most backlogged nationally — but emergency bond hearings can move quickly with immediate counsel", 'Los Angeles': "LA has the largest undocumented population of any US metro — a high-priority ICE enforcement zone in 2026. California's SB 54 limits local law enforcement cooperation but doesn't affect federal operations", 'Chicago': "Cook County's ordinance limits ICE detainer cooperation from local jails, but federal EOIR courts operate completely independently of local policy", 'Houston': "Houston's proximity to the southern border makes it one of the highest-priority ICE enforcement zones nationally — Harris County has seen elevated removal proceedings in 2026", 'Phoenix': "Arizona has no sanctuary policies — local law enforcement cooperates with ICE under the state's 287(g) programme, meaning any law enforcement contact can trigger immigration consequences", 'Dallas': 'Texas has no sanctuary policies and Dallas County cooperates with ICE detainers — any law enforcement contact can initiate federal immigration proceedings', 'Miami': "Miami's diverse immigrant community — Cuban, Venezuelan, Haitian, Colombian — each has distinct TPS designations and asylum pathways. Miami's bilingual immigration bar is highly experienced with nationality-specific cases", 'Seattle': "Washington State's sanctuary law limits local law enforcement ICE cooperation, providing additional procedural protections compared to Texas or Arizona", 'Denver': "Colorado's sanctuary bill limits local law enforcement ICE cooperation — local police cannot hold individuals solely on immigration detainers", 'Washington': "DC's strong sanctuary policies actively limit cooperation with federal immigration enforcement. DC Legal Aid and CAIR Coalition provide substantial free immigration legal services", 'Boston': 'Massachusetts has sanctuary policies. PAIR Project and Greater Boston Legal Services are among the strongest immigration legal aid resources of any US city', 'San Francisco': "SF's sanctuary policies are among the strongest nationally — local law enforcement will not assist ICE. The Bay Area has both a large professional visa community (H-1B, L-1) and large undocumented populations", 'Nashville': 'Tennessee has no sanctuary policies — Nashville area law enforcement cooperates with ICE. Any law enforcement contact can have immigration consequences for undocumented residents', 'Atlanta': 'Georgia operates the Stewart Detention Center — one of the largest immigration detention facilities in the country. Georgia has no sanctuary policies', 'Minneapolis': "Minnesota has limited sanctuary protections. Minneapolis's unique Somali and Hmong communities require attorneys with specific country-condition expertise for asylum cases", 'Charlotte': "North Carolina has no sanctuary policies and Mecklenburg County cooperates with ICE detainers. Charlotte's non-sanctuary status means any law enforcement contact can trigger proceedings", 'Indianapolis': 'Indiana has no sanctuary policies and local law enforcement cooperates with ICE. Indiana Legal Services provides free immigration help for qualifying low-income immigrants', 'Columbus': 'Columbus is a major refugee resettlement city — significant Somali, Latin American, Nepalese, and Bhutanese communities with distinct legal needs. Ohio has no sanctuary policies', 'Portland': "Oregon's sanctuary law prohibits state and local resources from being used for federal immigration enforcement — among the strongest protections nationally", 'San Antonio': "San Antonio's location within 150 miles of the US-Mexico border makes it a primary ICE enforcement hub. Texas has no sanctuary policies and Bexar County cooperates with ICE detainers"}
